From 5b36d4ddbe9bafbbcdba6a9085d353482a831d23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:03:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] test-posix: Check <syslog.h>, and keep test-syslog away
 from the system logger

test-syslog sent each message to /dev/log, the host's system log, as
well as standard error. It now runs in a child with no descriptor to
spare, so syslog can open neither its socket nor the console, and
checks %m with %n$, %%, the default mask, LOG_UPTO, facilities in the
mask test and later openlog calls. test-syslog_h checks the header in
strict XSI mode, and test-syslog-thread that a thread cancelled in
syslog leaves logging usable.
